Ladybird measures an automatically sized absolute box from its static-
position edge when both insets are auto. The normalized edge accounts
for direction and writing mode. The same rule applies to an orthogonal
child whose inline size is computed through the block-axis sizing path.
Its content-based block size is measured at the resolved inline size.

Blink resolves the edge in ComputeUnclampedIMCBInOneAxis(), before
ComputeInsetModifiedContainingBlock() supplies the available size.

Gecko selects a hypothetical inline-start or inline-end offset in its
ReflowInput::InitAbsoluteConstraints(), according to the writing modes.
It includes the offset in the space excluded by ComputeSize().

WebKit resolves the static-position edge for the appropriate writing
mode in PositionedLayoutConstraints::computeStaticPosition(). Its
computeInsets() subtracts the insets from the containing range.

These paths agree on measuring from the static-position edge before
shrink-to-fit sizing. Center-aligned static rectangles retain their
separate sizing behavior; this change covers start and end alignment.
